useLine:
    line = getCurrentLine()
    pattern = matchPattern(line)
    pattern.{opcode, operands[]}
    pattern.operand.{regexToGetItFromTheLine, types[]}
    each operands[].literal = regexToGetItFromTheLine(line)
    if not operand.type.recognize(literal) then error
    else each operands[].value = type.parseValue(literal)
    function[opcode](operands[].value)

FOR EACH LINE:
get the line
check if it matches one pattern
    if it matches none, throw an error
    if it matches one, good
    if it matches multiple, throw a warning and use the one with the highest priority
use that pattern to get the opcode and the operands
for each operand
    check if it matches one type pattern among its allowed types
        same logic as above
    parse the value according to its type
return the opcode and the operands, preferably named